Review-status check: the published verdict note does not cover every cold reviewer finding the prompt listed. Ids missing from the note body: {ids}.
- Publish the verdict again as `glab mr note <N> -m "…"` with a body that has one line per finding — its id and a verdict (fixed | open | refuted) — and the same single marker `<!-- verdict:approve|changes sha=<SHA> -->` on the same `<SHA>`. Pass the body in the command itself (one `-m "…"`, or `-m "$(cat <<'EOF' … EOF)"` for several lines): the hook does not read a body from a file.
- Then repeat your full verdict reply as your final message, its first line starting with 🟢 or 🔴 — only the final message reaches the user.
